  if (it.case) { const d = cleanCase(it.case); if (/^form:.*@\d+$/.test(d.importKey || '')) d.importKey = d.importKey.replace(/@\d+$/, '@' + d.updatedAt); b.set(...d) }
(or pass the commit-time stamp into a helper in form-inbox.js that builds both). Add a unit test that runs commitFormPickup against a fake SDK whose commits advance the clock (for example one 30 s stall, then several entries), then sends an edited response and checks that the edit is saved and not kept.
